[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    181[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Divergences found and fixed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    182[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    183[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Two real translation defects were found by these rows and fixed in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    184[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `translation/src/lib.rs` (the C was never modified):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    185[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    186[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **`c2BBVerts` — aliasing read order** (row 21). The Rust cached `bb->min`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    187[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    and `bb->max` into locals before writing any output, whereas the C re-reads
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    188[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `bb` between each of the four stores:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    189[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    190[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    out[0] = bb->min;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    191[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    out[1] = c2V(bb->max.x, bb->min.y);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    192[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    out[2] = bb->max;                    /* re-reads bb, possibly after out[1] overwrote it */
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    193[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    out[3] = c2V(bb->min.x, bb->max.y);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    194[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    195[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    With `out` overlapping `*bb` the two diverged on the very first case
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    196[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`out[2]`: C `(9.5, 4.0)` vs Rust `(9.5, 9.627013)`). Fixed by reading each
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    197[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    field through a raw pointer at the exact point of use.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    198[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    199[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. **`c2Witness` — borrow held across aliasing writes**. The Rust held
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    200[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `&(*s).verts` while storing through `*a`, which may alias the simplex. The
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    201[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    observable ordering happened to be correct under both `-O0` and `-O2`, but
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    202[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    the shared reference is invalidated by the write, so LLVM was free to hoist
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    203[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    the later loads above it. Rewritten with raw-pointer reads, matching the C's
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    204[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    read-after-write ordering unconditionally.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    205[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    206[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Build-flag sensitivity (not a translation defect)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    207[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    208[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The suite was additionally run against the C library rebuilt out-of-tree at
